    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the product of the greatest common divisor (GCD) and the least common multiple (LCM) of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\), we will first calculate the GCD. Then, we will find the LCM using the relationship between GCD and LCM. Finally, we will compute the product of the GCD and LCM.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution\n\n1. **Finding the GCD of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\)**:\n   We apply the Euclidean algorithm (the iterative process to find the GCD using division and the remainder).\n\n   - First, perform the division of \\(42\\) by \\(18\\):\n     \\[\n     42 = 18 \\cdot 2 + 6\n     \\]\n     So, the remainder is \\(6\\).\n\n   - Next, we make the divisor \\( 18 \\) and the remainder \\( 6 \\) and apply the division:\n     \\[\n     18 = 6 \\cdot 3 + 0\n     \\]\n     The remainder is \\(0\\), which means the GCD of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\) is \\(6\\).\n\n2. **Finding the LCM of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\)**:\n   Using the relationship between \\(\\text{GCD}\\) and \\(\\text{LCM}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{LCM}(a, b) = \\frac{a \\cdot b}{\\text{GCD}(a, b)}\n   \\]\n\n   Substituting \\(a = 18\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = \\frac{18 \\cdot 42}{\\text{GCD}(18, 42)}\n   \\]\n\n    \\[\n    \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = \\frac{18 \\cdot 42}{6}\n    \\]\n\n   \\[\n    \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = \\frac{756}{6}\n    \\]\n\n   \\[\n    \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = 126\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculating the product of the GCD and the LCM**:\n   We now find the product of \\( \\text{GCD}(18, 42) \\) and the \\(\\text{LCM}(18, 42)\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Product} = \\text{GCD}(18, 42) \\times \\text{LCM}(18, 42)\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Product} = 6 \\times 126\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Product} = 756\n   \\]\n\nPutting it all together, the product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\) is \\( \\boxed{756} \\).",
